[Music]  major league baseball season has been  pushed back until at least april 14th  when negotiations stalled over the new  collective bargaining agreement the  baseball commissioner canceled another  93 games yesterday in communities that  rely on spring training tourism a  billion dollar business have empty  stadiums and are getting hit hard chris  vancleave is outside globe life field in  arlington texas  chris um i guess we're not singing take  me out to the ball game anytime soon  no there's no singing at all in fact the  rangers had hoped to start their season  here in less than a month and fans were  really hoping for just a sense of  normalcy a spring training without  capacity restrictions without mask  mandates and local businesses were  hoping for a much needed boost now all  of that is on hold but this time it is  not the pandemic that's threatening to  keep the boys of summer benched  the stands at ed smith field in sarasota  will be empty once again today the  spring training home of the baltimore  orioles should be buzzing with excited  fans soaking up the florida sun and 45  minutes south the world champion braves  are also yet to take the field at their  spring training home in venice florida  we definitely are looking forward to  watching the braves instead we found  these fans outside the locked gates of  cool today park on what should have been  their first time at a spring training  game well it's disappointing because  it's my day off it's my son's day off  and we wanted to come and see a game but  it looks like the politics got the best  of us here spring training is big  business the florida grapefruit league  draws around 1.5 million fans generating  nearly 700 million dollars in arizona  the cactus league rakes in about 644  million from 1.8 million fans more than  half from out of state it's very  frustrating for the business community  heather caston is the president and ceo  of the greater sarasota chamber of  commerce she says spring training is  worth about 63 million dollars to local  businesses and the orioles generate  roughly 500 seasonal jobs the people who  are working at the stadium who maybe  this is their second or third job  those you know the people who support  all of the services that go along with  spring training  they're the folks that are going to be  impacted also impacted mike quillen's  geckos grill and pub restaurants it's  kind of the gravy on top of everything  that we really look forward to  to to it every year it's certainly not  been the best time to be in the  restaurant business a little extra  sounds pretty good right now  a little extra sounds great but uh you  know it's been a challenging a  challenging two years major league  baseball says if there is a season it  wants four weeks of spring training but  that can't happen until there's a deal  with the players putting a nearly 11  billion dollar business at risk  baseball's last labor breakdown led the  cancellation of the 1994 world series  attendance didn't fully recover for more  than a decade is there a risk to  baseball that  the millionaires negotiating with  billionaires  alienates the fans yes of course it does  and especially when you negotiate the  public and you remind each everybody  each day how much money you all make it  alienates the casual  fan and that's that's where the damage  gets done that's why they have to do  this deal now and they know it  chabon who you just heard from there was  the general manager of the cincinnati  reds back in 1994 he says the biggest  difference between now and then casual  fans have a lot of entertainment options  many of them right here on their phone  so baseball could be singing the blues  nate for years to come  see what you did there chris thank you  so much

